<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The pre-Android-12 splash.

  Android 12 and up ignore this entirely and use the windowSplashScreen* items
  in styles.xml instead; this is the fallback for everything older, which is
  still most EGX users' phones. Both paths are handed the same mark and the
  same background so they cannot drift apart.

  splash_logo IS THE REAL BRAND MARK NOW, not a stand-in. It used to be a
  hand-drawn radar scope — three rings and a sweep — justified by a comment
  claiming assets/logo.png "still reads TradeMind" and was "a JPEG with no
  alpha". Neither was true any more: the file is a 1024px PNG of the actual
  lime R. So the launch screen showed one logo and the launcher icon showed a
  different one, which is the sort of thing nobody reports and everybody
  notices.

  It is now generated from that same PNG by tool/gen-splash-logo.mjs, which
  drops the dark plate so the mark sits directly on the charcoal field, and
  pads it to 62% so Android 12's circular mask cannot clip it.

  `<item>` with gravity and an explicit size, NOT `<bitmap>`: this keeps
  working whether splash_logo is a raster or a vector. Item gravity and sizing
  need API 23; minSdk here is 24.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:drawable="@color/splash_background" />
    <item
        android:drawable="@drawable/splash_logo"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:width="160dp"
        android:height="160dp" />
</layer-list>
